From e0cdadd1f5f71eef07f2bad9ed15fa2b673f76c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:20:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(workflow): add run snapshots and lookup by
 idempotency key

Callers of a WorkflowRuntime can only ask for the run status, so the
reconciler cannot read what a step produced (for a deployment: the
launched instance and its address) nor find the run of a resource
without calling start(), which creates and executes a run when none
exists. Deleting a resource must look for an in-flight deployment
without starting one.

Add RunInfo (status, step statuses in definition order, outputs of the
steps that succeeded, failure reason) and two non-abstract methods:
get_run(run_id), which defaults to the status only, and
find_run(idempotency_key), which has no side effects and raises
NotImplementedError unless a runtime implements it. The abstract
methods are unchanged, so existing runtimes such as the Temporal plugin
keep working; the additions are registered in a contract test.
